Anona Runners is in beta: behaviour and limits may change.

Run GitHub Actions jobs on Anona runners.

Install the Anona GitHub App on your organization with "runners connect", then
point a workflow at a size with runs-on: anona-small, anona-medium, anona-large
or anona-xl. Each job runs in a fresh sandbox of that size. A size above your
plan's limit is refused. Runners need a paid plan and private repositories.

Usage:
  anona-compute runners [flags]
  anona-compute runners [command]

Available Commands:
  connect     Install the GitHub App and link it to this workspace
  disconnect  Unlink a GitHub installation
  job         Show one runner job
  jobs        List recent runner jobs
  status      Show linked installations and the runs-on labels to use

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for runners

Global Flags:
      --api-key string             API key (env ANONA_COMPUTE_API_KEY, ANONA_API_KEY, E2B_API_KEY)
      --api-url string             API URL (env ANONA_COMPUTE_API_URL, E2B_API_URL; default https://api.<E2B_DOMAIN>)
      --json                       JSON output on stdout (same as -o json)
  -o, --output string              output format: text or json (default "text")
      --profile string             config profile to use (env ANONA_COMPUTE_PROFILE; default "default")
      --request-timeout duration   timeout for each non-streaming request, 0 = none (create, pause, resume and fork: 3m0s unless set; streams and uploads are never cut off) (default 1m0s)
  -v, --verbose                    verbose output on stderr

Use "anona-compute runners [command] --help" for more information about a command.
